    "json": [
      {
        "path": "count",
        "op": "eq",
        "value": 1
      },
      {
        "path": "xrefs[0].from_function.name",
        "op": "eq",
        "value": "_direct_goal"
      },
      {
        "path": "coverage.unwalked",
        "op": "len_eq",
        "value": 2
      },
      {
        "path": "coverage.unwalked[0].name",
        "op": "eq",
        "value": "_middle"
      },
      {
        "path": "coverage.unwalked[0].section",
        "op": "eq",
        "value": "__TEXT,__const"
      }
    ]
  },
  "notes": "GH-1406: `--to _goal` walks what it walked before, so _middle's call (from code in __TEXT,__const that no walk decodes by itself) is still not a row, but the answer names _middle (and _quiet, also called from _main) under coverage.unwalked instead of looking complete."
